WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.093 --> 00:00:04.440
Roscoe and Cleo talked for a while about the situation.

2
00:00:04.441 --> 00:00:09.114
It was unfortunate, but it was also true.

3
00:00:09.115 --> 00:00:13.294
They had no proof those two cats stole the jewels.

4
00:00:13.295 --> 00:00:19.719
Cleo unlocked the jail cell. "Go on. Get out of here."

5
00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:23.097
"Truly?" Violet asked.

6
00:00:23.098 --> 00:00:27.929
Cleo nodded. "We can't prove you stole the jewels."

7
00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:33.835
"Don't let us catch you in Prickly Pear again," Roscoe said.

8
00:00:33.836 --> 00:00:44.292
Sasha and Violet walked out of the jail cell.

9
00:00:44.293 --> 00:00:49.513
They giggled as they left the sheriff's office.

10
00:00:49.514 --> 00:00:54.100
*** "I can't believe how easy that was," Violet

11
00:00:54.101 --> 00:00:58.225
said. "That sheriff and deputy sure are

12
00:00:58.226 --> 00:01:09.353
dumb!" Sasha laughed. "Let's go dig up our jewels!"

13
00:01:09.354 --> 00:01:15.929
The two cats hiked up into the hills and found Zeke's shovel.

14
00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:20.219
They went to the spot where the jewels were buried.

15
00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:24.209
The thieves took turns digging.

16
00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:30.485
Finally they heard the shovel hit something hard.

17
00:01:30.486 --> 00:01:34.883
Sasha grinned. "There's the trunk!"

18
00:01:34.884 --> 00:01:40.112
They pulled it out of the dirt and set it down.

19
00:01:40.113 --> 00:01:45.240
"Now we have all the proof we need!" a voice said.

20
00:01:45.241 --> 00:01:49.601
Sasha and Violet spun around and gasped.

21
00:01:49.602 --> 00:01:52.773
That deputy was standing over them!

22
00:01:52.774 --> 00:01:55.691
The sheriff appeared behind her.

23
00:01:55.692 --> 00:01:59.802
Both law officers had their slingshots drawn.

24
00:01:59.803 --> 00:02:03.348
"We'll take that trunk," Roscoe said.

25
00:02:03.349 --> 00:02:10.192
"How did you find us?" Violet asked.

26
00:02:10.193 --> 00:02:13.681
"We followed you," Cleo said.

27
00:02:13.682 --> 00:02:19.026
"We knew you wouldn't leave town without the jewels."

28
00:02:19.027 --> 00:02:25.804
Roscoe smiled. "You led us right to them!"

29
00:02:25.805 --> 00:02:28.915
Sasha swung the shovel at the law officers.

30
00:02:28.916 --> 00:02:33.175
"Grab the trunk and run, Violet! I'll hold them off."

31
00:02:33.176 --> 00:02:36.663
Violet reached down to grab the trunk. Thwap!

32
00:02:36.664 --> 00:02:40.329
Cleo shot a rock at the ground near Violet's paw.

33
00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:44.688
"Yikes!" Violet pulled her paw back.

34
00:02:44.689 --> 00:02:47.546
Roscoe picked up the trunk.

35
00:02:47.547 --> 00:02:50.079
"You're under arrest."

36
00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:53.895
"No way!" Sasha raised the shovel.

37
00:02:53.896 --> 00:03:00.076
Thwap! Thwap! Thwap! Cleo hit it with rocks until she dropped it. "Okay!"

38
00:03:00.077 --> 00:03:04.459
Sasha shouted. "I surrender!" Violet

39
00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:11.882
sighed. "Me too." ***

40
00:03:11.883 --> 00:03:18.410
The next morning the federal marshals arrived.

41
00:03:18.411 --> 00:03:21.930
They boarded the train with the jewels and the thieves.

42
00:03:21.931 --> 00:03:32.163
Cleo and Roscoe watched the train pull out of the station.

43
00:03:32.164 --> 00:03:37.048
"Sorry I didn't realize those two were trouble," Cleo said.

44
00:03:37.049 --> 00:03:40.853
"I guess I just wanted to make some new friends."

45
00:03:40.854 --> 00:03:47.039
Roscoe shrugged. "Sometimes folks who seem good are actually bad."

46
00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:53.751
He looked at Cleo. "Other times, folks who were bad are actually pretty great."

47
00:03:53.752 --> 00:03:57.447
Cleo smiled. "Thanks, Sheriff."

48
00:03:57.448 --> 00:04:10.945
Then she yawned. It was about time for a nap.

